    "sourceText": "Azerbaijan, located at the crossroads of Europe and Asia, is a destination rich in history, \nculture, and natural beauty. From the bustling streets of Baku to the serene Caspian Sea \ncoastline, Azerbaijan offers a variety of experiences for every type of traveller. Whether you \nare drawn to its ancient architecture, vibrant nightlife, or stunning landscapes, Azerbaijan \nhas something for everyone. \n \n Indian nationals require a valid visa to enter Azerbaijan. The type of visa needed depends \non the purpose of the visit. However, before you pack your bags and explore this captivating \ncountry, it\u2019s important to understand the visa requirements. All travellers, regardless of \nnationality, will need to obtain a visa before entering Azerbaijan. \nTypes of Azerbaijan Visa \nSelecting the correct visa category helps ensure a smooth and successful application process \nfor Indian travellers planning to visit Azerbaijan. \n \nAzerbaijan Tourist Visa (Short Stay \u2013 Single Entry) \nThe Azerbaijan Tourist Visa is suitable for Indian travellers visiting Azerbaijan for holidays, \nsightseeing, cultural exploration, or meeting friends and family. \nThis visa allows a short stay and requires applicants to submit hotel bookings, a confirmed \nreturn itinerary, financial proof, and a valid passport. It is commonly issued as an e-visa, \nmaking the application process quick and convenient for Indian travellers. \n \nAzerbaijan Business Visa (Short Stay \u2013 Single Entry) \nThe Azerbaijan Business Visa is designed for Indian citizens travelling to Azerbaijan for \nbusiness meetings, conferences, trade fairs, corporate visits, or professional events. \nApplicants must provide an invitation letter from the host company in Azerbaijan along with \nsupporting business and financial documents. Like the tourist visa, the business visa is often \navailable as an e-visa, allowing easier processing for short-term business travel. \n \nDocuments Required for Azerbaijan visa application: \n \nVisa Type \n \nDocuments Required  \n \nAzerbaijan eVisa - Priority \n \nThis express service assures visa processing within 3 working hours after submission to the \nembassy. \n \nFront and back colour scanned copies of new & old passports. \nHolding a valid passport with a validity of more than three months. \nConfirmed hotel voucher and itinerary. \nReturn flight tickets. (Optional) \nAzerbaijan standard e-Visa \n \nFront and back colour scan copies of new & old passports. \nHolding a valid passport with a validity of more than three months. \nConfirmed hotel voucher and itinerary. \nInvitation letter from the invitee's company. \nReturn flight tickets. (Optional) \nAzerbaijan eVisa - Priority  \n \nThis express service assures visa processing within 3 working hours after submission to the \nembassy. \n \nFront and back colour scan copies of new & old passports. \nHolding a valid passport with a validity of more than three months. \nConfirmed hotel voucher and itinerary. \nReturn flight tickets. (Optional) \nAzerbaijan standard e-Visa \n \nFront and back colour scan copies of new & old passports. \nHolding a valid passport with a validity of more than three months. \nConfirmed hotel voucher and itinerary. \nReturn flight tickets. (Optional) \n Points to Note \nApplications are liable to be rejected if the uploaded documents and photograph are not \nclear or as per the given specification. \nAny applicant may be asked to provide additional documents as per the embassy\u2019s \ndiscretion. \nAdditional time may be required by the Embassy depending on the visa application process. \nVisa-on-arrival in Azerbaijan \nAzerbaijan does not offer a visa-on-arrival option for most travellers. Indian citizens must \nobtain an Azerbaijan visa before travelling. Nationals from some countries may have visa \nexemptions or be eligible for a visa on arrival, but Indian travellers need to apply for an eVisa \nor obtain a visa from the Azerbaijan Embassy/Consulate in advance for tourism or business \npurposes."
