    "sourceText": "Italy offers a rich tapestry of experiences. With an enchanting blend of history, art, and \nculinary delights, this destination is a must-visit for tourists. \n \nIndian citizens planning to visit Italy must apply for an Italy Tourist Visa in advance. \n \nAn Italy visa for Indians serves as a Schengen short stay visa, and entitles the visa holder to \nvisit the Schengen countries for Tourism, or other non-business-related purposes for up to \n90 days within a 180-day period from date of first entry. \nTypes of Italy Visa \nItaly offers various types of visas depending on the purpose of your visit. Each visa type has \nspecific documentation and eligibility criteria for the visa you intend to apply for. \n \nSchengen Visa (Short-Stay Visa - Type C) \n \nItaly Business Visa \n \nIf you are travelling for attending business meetings, conferences, or trade fairs, you can \napply for an Italy Business Visa. \n \nItaly Tourist Visa \n \nYou can apply for an Italy Tourist Visa if you wish to enter the country for sightseeing, visiting \nfamily or friends, or attending events. \n \nTake an Italy visa appointment and begin planning your Italian getaway. \n \nDocuments Required for Italy visa application: \n \nVisa Type \n \nDocuments Required \n \nItaly Business Visa \n \nApplication form duly filled and signed by the applicant. \nTwo recent photos in the size of 35X45 mm with white background 80% face. \nOriginal passport - valid for at least three months with minimum 2 blank pages. \nAll previous passports and proof of loss passport (if any) \nThe passport should be issued less than 10 years ago. \nCopies of all previous Schengen visas with stamps, valid USA and UK visas If any. \nOriginal covering letter on company letterhead signed and stamped with purpose of travel, \ndesignation, passport details and date of travel. \nCompany Registration Certificate/ Memorandum of articles. \nFor self-employed citizens - Certificate of Incorporation. \nOriginal Invitation letter from invitee company letterhead signed and stamped with purpose \nof travel, passport details, designation, invitee name and date of travel. \nLOI needs to be sent via email by the inviting company to commerciale.mumbai@esteri.it \nbefore processing submission at VAC centre. (original or coloured copy) \nCopy of the Passport or Identity card of the person in Italy who is signing the invitation letter. \nCopy of the Visura Camerale of the inviting Company (Registration with the local Chamber of \ncommerce) dated not less than six months prior to the intended travel. \nNOC from company. \nFinancial documents: \nLast 3 months' salary slips. \nIncome Tax Acknowledgement for last three years. \nLast six-month bank statements with stamp and signature on it. \nTravel insurance - medical coverage minimum Euro 30,000. Minimum 10 days insurance is \nmandatory from the travel date in Schengen. \nConfirmed hotel voucher and airline return tickets. \nItaly Tourist Visa \n \nApplication form duly filled and signed by the applicant. \nTwo recent photos in the size of 35X45 mm with white background 80% face. \nOriginal passport - valid for at least three months with minimum 2 blank pages. \nAll previous passports and proof of lost passport (if any) \nThe passport should be issued less than 10 years ago. \nCopies of all previous Schengen visa with stamps, valid USA and UK visas, if any. \nOriginal covering letter signed by applicant with purpose of travel, designation, passport \ndetails, travel expenses and date of travel. \nCompany Registration Certificate/ Memorandum of articles. \nIn case of self-employed - Certificate of Incorporation. \nNOC from company. \nFinancial documents: \nLast 3 months' salary slips. \nIncome Tax Acknowledgement for last three years. \nLast six-month bank statements with stamp and signature on it. \nTravel insurance - medical coverage minimum Euro 30,000. Minimum 10 days insurance is \nmandatory from the travel date in Schengen. \nConfirmed hotel voucher and flight return tickets. \nProof of all internal travels within the Schengen territory including train bookings, car rentals \nif any. \nFor sponsors: Proof of sponsorship and a letter from the sponsor, financial documents as \nwell as copy of the sponsor\u2019s photo ID, (e.g. passport, Aadhaar card or driver\u2019s license) \nIn case of retired - Pension statements for last 3 months or proof of regular income \ngenerated by ownership of property or business. \nMinor Applicants:  \nNOC from School/University \nCopy of Birth Certificate \nSponsorship Letter & expenses, Parent\u2019s Marriage Certificate \nParental Authorization (If Minor is travelling alone) \nPlease note: \nAny applicant may be asked to provide additional documents as per Embassy\u2019s discretion. \nProcessing days will be calculated once all documents have been submitted in accordance \nwith the embassy requirements. \n \nIs there visa-on-arrival in Italy? \nItaly does not offer visa-on-arrival option for most travellers. Depending on your nationality, \na Schengen visa must be obtained before travelling. Citizens of EU countries, USA, Canada, \nAustralia, and some other countries can enter Italy without a visa for short stays (up to 90 \ndays) for tourism or business purposes."
